## ***********************************************************************
## **
## **  THEME.INC.BL -- named colour roles, in five themes.
## **
## **  The colours are an array, read by BASIC for COLOR and the GP drawing
## **  commands, so they save and load like any other.
## **
## **      THEME.ID%  0 X16       blue page, white text -- the default
## **                 1 DARK      black page, light grey text
## **                 2 LIGHT     white page, black text
## **                 3 GRAY      dark grey page, light blue frames
## **                 4 CUSTOM    whatever THEME.CLR already holds
## **
## **  THEME.NEXT cycles to the following one and loads it, which is what a
## **  program binds to a key. THEME.RESET reloads the one already selected.
## **
## **  THEME.STAMP% counts the loads. A module that copies colours out of THEME.CLR
## **  keeps the stamp it copied at and re-reads when the two differ, so a theme
## **  change reaches it with nothing asked of the program.
## **
## **  CUSTOM loads nothing, leaving THEME.CLR as it stands, so a program that lets
## **  the user change colours carries those changes into it. Selected before any
## **  other theme it takes X16's values.
## **
## **  Usage:
## **      THEME.ID% = 1 : GOSUB THEME.SELECT
## **      GP.BOX 4,2,30,8, 2, THEME.CLR(THEME.BORDER)
## **      GP.PRINTAT 6,3, "TITLE", THEME.CLR(THEME.TITLE)
## **
## **  The values are packed attributes, background * 16 + foreground, as the GP
## **  drawing commands take them. For COLOR, which wants the halves separately,
## **  use THEME.SET.
## **
## **  THE MODULE'S OWN SCALARS CARRY %, THE ARRAY DOES NOT. An untyped scalar is six
## **  bytes of the 4,096-byte variable arena and an int16 is two, so the six scalars
## **  here are 24 bytes of it. That arena is what raises TOO MANY VARIABLES, and it is
## **  a different budget from the free memory the banner calls LOW FREE. THEME.CLR is
## **  read by name in every module that draws, so typing it would rename ninety-odd
## **  call sites to buy array elements, which come out of LOW FREE instead.
## **
## **  TO RUN IT FROM A RAM BANK, put the #INCLUDE between GP.BANKED and
## **  GP.ENDBANKED. A call from outside the region selects the region's bank
## **  and RETURN puts the caller's back, so a caller is written the same
## **  either way. GPC-BASIC/BANKED-OR-NOT.md has the rules.
## **
## ***********************************************************************
#IFNDEF THEME.DEFS
#DEFINE THEME.DEFS 1

## The roles. Add one here and to ALL FIVE palettes below, and raise SLOTS.
##
## FOCUS IS NOT HILITE, and it exists because it could not be. HILITE is the
## text colour reversed in three of the four palettes, and a GUI button is drawn
## as the panel reversed, so a focused button came out identical to a plain one.
## FOCUS is yellow-backed in every theme for that reason: whatever a palette
## does, nothing else in it is yellow.
##
## BAR is a menu bar or status line: a background of its own, so the band
## stands off the page. BORDER's colour marks a hot key on it.
##
## SHADOW is the colour a drop shadow is filled with -- a menu's, a dialog's --
## and it is black on every palette. It is a role rather than a constant so that
## a program which changes its colours changes this one with them.

#DEFINE THEME.PAGE 0
#DEFINE THEME.TEXT 1
#DEFINE THEME.TITLE 2
#DEFINE THEME.BORDER 3
#DEFINE THEME.HILITE 4
#DEFINE THEME.DIMMED 5
#DEFINE THEME.WARN 6
#DEFINE THEME.FOCUS 7
#DEFINE THEME.BAR 8
#DEFINE THEME.SHADOW 9
#DEFINE THEME.SLOTS 10

## How many themes THEME.NEXT cycles through.
#DEFINE THEME.COUNT 5

## X16 palette indices, for reading the tables below.
##   0 black    1 white   2 red     3 cyan     4 purple  5 green
##   6 blue     7 yellow  8 orange  9 brown   10 pink   11 dk grey
##  12 md grey 13 lt green 14 lt blue 15 lt grey

GOTO THEME.SKIP

## THE PALETTES HOLD THE PACKED NUMBER, NOT background * 16 + foreground. The compiler
## folds no constants, so 6 * 16 + 14 emits five bytes of p-code and does the multiply
## every time a theme loads, where 110 emits two. The comment above each palette carries
## the background and foreground pair every number was built from.

## THEME.SELECT -- fill THEME.CLR from THEME.ID%.
##
## THEME.CLR is DIMmed here, because DIMming an array GPC has already auto-dimensioned
## is an error. The bound is THEME.SLOTS - 1: DIM X(n) gives n+1 elements and the roles
## run 0..THEME.SLOTS-1, so DIMming to THEME.SLOTS allocated an element nobody writes.
## No DATA statement, because READ walks every DATA in the whole program in order and a
## library owning one would derail the caller's READs.
##
## SHADOW is black in all four palettes, so it is written once here rather than four
## times below. CUSTOM must keep the colours it already has, so it turns back before
## that line -- except on the pass that created the array, which has nothing to keep
## and falls through to X16 like any other first load.

THEME.SELECT:
    THEME.STAMP% = THEME.STAMP% + 1
    THEME.FIRST% = 0
    IF THEME.READY% = 0 THEN DIM THEME.CLR(THEME.SLOTS - 1) : THEME.READY% = -1 : THEME.FIRST% = -1
    IF THEME.ID% = 4 AND THEME.FIRST% = 0 THEN RETURN
    THEME.CLR(THEME.SHADOW) = 0
    IF THEME.ID% = 1 THEN GOTO THEME.SELECT.DARK
    IF THEME.ID% = 2 THEN GOTO THEME.SELECT.LIGHT
    IF THEME.ID% = 3 THEN GOTO THEME.SELECT.GRAY

## page 6,6   text 6,1   title 6,3   border 6,14   hilite 1,6
## dimmed 6,12   warn 6,13   focus 7,6   bar 12,1
THEME.SELECT.X16:
    THEME.CLR(THEME.PAGE)   = 102
    THEME.CLR(THEME.TEXT)   = 97
    THEME.CLR(THEME.TITLE)  = 99
    THEME.CLR(THEME.BORDER) = 110
    THEME.CLR(THEME.HILITE) = 22
    THEME.CLR(THEME.DIMMED) = 108
    THEME.CLR(THEME.WARN)   = 109
    THEME.CLR(THEME.FOCUS)  = 118
    THEME.CLR(THEME.BAR)    = 193
    RETURN

## page 0,0   text 0,15   title 0,1   border 0,11   hilite 15,0
## dimmed 0,12   warn 0,8   focus 7,0   bar 6,1
THEME.SELECT.DARK:
    THEME.CLR(THEME.PAGE)   = 0
    THEME.CLR(THEME.TEXT)   = 15
    THEME.CLR(THEME.TITLE)  = 1
    THEME.CLR(THEME.BORDER) = 11
    THEME.CLR(THEME.HILITE) = 240
    THEME.CLR(THEME.DIMMED) = 12
    THEME.CLR(THEME.WARN)   = 8
    THEME.CLR(THEME.FOCUS)  = 112
    THEME.CLR(THEME.BAR)    = 97
    RETURN

## A white page. DIMMED is mid grey rather than dark grey so that reversing it
## for a status bar still leaves the text readable on it.
##
## page 1,1   text 1,0   title 1,6   border 1,11   hilite 0,1
## dimmed 1,12   warn 1,2   focus 7,0   bar 15,0
THEME.SELECT.LIGHT:
    THEME.CLR(THEME.PAGE)   = 17
    THEME.CLR(THEME.TEXT)   = 16
    THEME.CLR(THEME.TITLE)  = 22
    THEME.CLR(THEME.BORDER) = 27
    THEME.CLR(THEME.HILITE) = 1
    THEME.CLR(THEME.DIMMED) = 28
    THEME.CLR(THEME.WARN)   = 18
    THEME.CLR(THEME.FOCUS)  = 112
    THEME.CLR(THEME.BAR)    = 240
    RETURN

## From the XFMGR file manager's theme module. DIMMED and WARN are not in it.
##
## WARN IS LIGHT RED, NOT RED. This is the only theme with a dark grey page, and
## plain red on it is barely legible. BAR is mid grey, one step lighter than the page,
## rather than the blue it used to be: a blue band over a grey page belongs to no theme.
##
## page 11,11   text 11,1   title 11,7   border 11,14   hilite 14,1
## dimmed 11,12   warn 11,10   focus 7,11   bar 12,1
THEME.SELECT.GRAY:
    THEME.CLR(THEME.PAGE)   = 187
    THEME.CLR(THEME.TEXT)   = 177
    THEME.CLR(THEME.TITLE)  = 183
    THEME.CLR(THEME.BORDER) = 190
    THEME.CLR(THEME.HILITE) = 225
    THEME.CLR(THEME.DIMMED) = 188
    THEME.CLR(THEME.WARN)   = 186
    THEME.CLR(THEME.FOCUS)  = 123
    THEME.CLR(THEME.BAR)    = 193
    RETURN

## THEME.NEXT -- the following theme, selected. It GOTOs THEME.SELECT rather than
## GOSUBing it, so THEME.SELECT's RETURN is the one the caller gets.
THEME.NEXT:
    THEME.ID% = THEME.ID% + 1 : IF THEME.ID% >= THEME.COUNT THEN THEME.ID% = 0
    GOTO THEME.SELECT

## THEME.RESET -- the selected theme's shipped values, throwing away any changes.
## CUSTOM has none of its own, so it resets to X16 -- and writes SHADOW on the way,
## because that jump lands past the line in THEME.SELECT which would have written it.
THEME.RESET:
    THEME.STAMP% = THEME.STAMP% + 1
    IF THEME.ID% = 4 THEN THEME.CLR(THEME.SHADOW) = 0 : GOTO THEME.SELECT.X16
    GOTO THEME.SELECT

## THEME.SET -- make THEME.ATTR% the colour PRINT uses.
##
##   in   THEME.ATTR%   a packed attribute, e.g. THEME.CLR(THEME.TEXT)
##
## WARNING: AND 15 is safe only because a packed attribute is 0..255. AND is 16-bit
## signed and raises OUT OF RANGE above 32767.

THEME.SET:
    COLOR THEME.ATTR% AND 15, INT(THEME.ATTR% / 16)
    RETURN

## THEME.HI -- the inverse of a packed attribute, for pre-drawing a row that should
## already look selected.
##
##   in   THEME.ATTR%   packed attribute      out  THEME.INV%

THEME.HI:
    THEME.INV% = (THEME.ATTR% AND 15) * 16 + INT(THEME.ATTR% / 16)
    RETURN

THEME.SKIP:
#ENDIF
